# Generated run artifacts stay out of git — prompts, responses, requests and
# blackboards are bulky machine output, reproducible from the pipeline.
#
# The EXCEPTIONS below are not machine output. They are Max's editorial
# judgement and the record of what he judged, and they existed in exactly one
# place: this disk. `rules.json` carries the rules distilled from them, but the
# evidence behind every rule — the whole corpus `rubric.md` will be compiled
# from — was uninsured until 2026-08-05. A dead drive would have erased five
# days of irreplaceable judgement. So these are versioned with everything else:
#
#   feedback.jsonl  — every verdict, tag and note Max has written
#   decisions.jsonl — approve / reject / revise, and attempt outcomes
#   board.json      — the board each judgement is ABOUT (feedback references
#                     sets by id; without the board it is unreadable)
#   manifest.json   — theme, status, and `brief.mock`, which is what separates
#                     real editorial signal from a fixture replay
#
# ~400KB of text across ~20 runs. The bulk stays ignored.
#
# `!*/` comes first because git will not descend into an ignored directory:
# without it the negations below are never reached.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!feedback.jsonl
!decisions.jsonl
!manifest.json
!*/attempts/*/board.json
